U-Boot loader and related files for the Banana Pi BPI-R3, for booting
from the SD card (SW1 set to SD boot).

The boot ROM loads bl2.img from the GPT partition marked as legacy BIOS
bootable. BL2 then loads u-boot.fip, which holds BL31 and U-Boot, from
the GPT partition named "fip". U-Boot keeps its environment in the GPT
partition named "ubootenv".

To install this bootloader on an SD card where these partitions are
named "bl2" and "fip" just do:

cd /usr/local/share/u-boot/u-boot-bananapi-r3
dd if=bl2.img of=/dev/gpt/bl2 bs=512 conv=sync
dd if=u-boot.fip of=/dev/gpt/fip bs=512 conv=sync
